# Text Hygiene (ASCII)

## Goal

Keep docs/config text easy to diff and safe for tooling.

## Never introduce

Almost always paste artifacts, and they break tooling or hide inside diffs.
No file convention justifies them.

- Invisible characters: NBSP, zero-width, variation selectors.
- Smart quotes. Use `'` and `"`.

## Prefer, unless the file says otherwise

Prefer the ASCII hyphen (`-`) over en and em dashes, and plain ASCII over
decorative punctuation generally. New files start ASCII.

When the file being edited already carries a non-ASCII convention
consistently, match it. Prose that uses em dashes throughout stays that way:
a file mixing both conventions reads worse than either one, and the diff noise
of converting it costs more than the convention does.

## Scope

Edit the lines the task touches. Never sweep a file for punctuation you had no
other reason to change.

## Output discipline

Speak up only when the reader has to act: a `never introduce` character sitting
in existing content, or a replacement that would change meaning. Following the
file's existing convention is the expected outcome and needs no remark.
